Solution:
def is_Even(n) : 
    if (n^1 == n+1) :
        return True; 
    else :
        return False;

Task: Write a function to find the minimum cost path to reach (m, n) from (0, 0) for the given cost matrix cost[][] and a position (m, n) in cost[][].
Solution:
R = 3
C = 3
def min_cost(cost, m, n): 
	tc = [[0 for x in range(C)] for x in range(R)] 
	tc[0][0] = cost[0][0] 
	for i in range(1, m+1): 
		tc[i][0] = tc[i-1][0] + cost[i][0] 
	for j in range(1, n+1): 
		tc[0][j] = tc[0][j-1] + cost[0][j] 
	for i in range(1, m+1): 
		for j in range(1, n+1): 
			tc[i][j] = min(tc[i-1][j-1], tc[i-1][j], tc[i][j-1]) + cost[i][j] 
	return tc[m][n]

